      "id": "d625da6619d4049d8e139b33213672684a25f851",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1703: the stage counts its own bodies\n\nFound by the contrary walker on the Harpy of the Cradle of Dusk\n(interrupted road, sweeps two and three; the same class broke the\nSludge Behemoth's brood probe earlier). The walker stepped onto the\nCradle of Dusk at stage 3 - four Aetheric Ravens, an ambush - and a\ncorruption apparition (\"The aether under your skin draws something out\n- Aetheric Raven forms from the haze\") stood there first. The arrival\narm keeps its door while a live hostile is on the tile, so the brood\nwaited; the walker killed the one apparition raven; and the escort clear\nin resolveStageEscortClear matched the stage by NAME alone\n(spawn.enemyName === enemy.name), found nothing else standing, and moved\nthe hunt on: \"The last of them is down.\" Four ravens the stage promised\nnever existed. A player who meets any same-named wanderer on a spawn\nstage's ground gets the beat for free - or, on the flee-return path,\ngets it stolen by a passer-by.\n\nFix: the stage tags the bodies it stands up. spawnStageEscort takes the\nencounter key (`family:id:stage` - the key missionEncounters already\nuses) and writes it onto every body as Enemy.stageKey; the escort clear\ncredits a death only when the dying body carries the stage's key, and\ncounts \"still up\" by that key too. A wanderer of the same name is a\nwanderer. The deferred arm then fires on the clear field (the per-action\ndoor, the dice-path re-arm) and stands up the four ravens it owed.\n\nA scene saved mid-escort before this OTA holds keyless bodies; those no\nlonger close the stage. Once they fall the arrival door stands the stage's\nown pack up, so the fight is fought once more on the day of the update,\nand the hunt stays finishable. Documented in the type and the clear.\n\nSuite ota1703TheStageCountsItsOwnBodies (store-level, the harpy at stage\n3 on the Cradle): a keyless Aetheric Raven's death leaves the record on\nstage 3; a body carrying the stage's key advances it; the stand-up\nthrough advanceHunt writes the key on all four bodies; source pins on the\ntag and the match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-06T00:18:40Z",
